  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nA closed upper-level low over the West Coast this weekend will \ndig southeastward across the Intermountain West Sunday night \ninto the Central and Southern Plains Monday, inducing surface \ncyclogenesis over Colorado and Kansas. The upper low is \nprojected to stall and slowly meander eastward across the \nmid/lower Mississippi Valley through midweek, ejecting several \nlobes of vorticity ahead of this feature and supporting daily \nchances for showers and a few storms through at least the first \nhalf of next week. NBM probabilities for reaching at least an \ninch of rain in 48-hours peak around 60% west of I-57 Wednesday \nevening/night. Mild temperatures in the upper 60s and 70s will \ndominate early to midweek. \n\nTiming differences between the models persist but are starting \nto hone in on the surface low and attendant cold front passing \nthrough central Illinois Wednesday night into Thursday. High \ntemperatures drop into the 40s and 50s in the wake of the system\nunder a period of blustery northerly winds. Given the continued\ntiming discrepancies among models, the NBM currently broad- \nbrushes the thermal gradient late in the week averaging out the \nforecast highs in the 60s.",
